  "subject": "A seal-carver's apprentice must carve his girlfriend Huē-bûn's name in mirror writing and has ruined ninety-nine stones, so on the hundredth he presses it first on his own palm.",
  "caption": "Brazilian MPB-style ballad in the Taiwanese Hokkien language, gently swaying syncopated bossa-adjacent pulse. Nylon-string guitar with fingerstyle syncopation and rich jazz-tinged chords, upright bass, soft shaker and cajon brushes, a solo flute answering the vocal, felt piano in the bridge. Warm close-miked acoustic room with light plate reverb. Male vocal, soft clear mid-register tenor, gentle sincere delivery, clearly sung melody. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 74 BPM, G major. Tender, patient, quietly smiling mood. No drum kit, no electric guitar, no synth, no autotune, no rap.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n石頭一粒，刀仔一支\n我欲刻伊的名，惠雯\n字愛倒反來刻，印出來才是正\n我已經刻壞九十九粒\n[Pre-Chorus]\n一刀落去，我毋敢喘氣\n刀鋒偏一絲，伊的名就變款\n[Chorus]\n惠雯，惠雯，我倒寫你的名\n倒寫的字，印出來才是正\n我的心事若有人用鏡來照\n就會當讀著，是你\n[Verse]\n師傅講，你的手穩，心袂穩\n九十九粒石頭，排佇桌頂\n有的少一點，有的倒一撇\n有的字真媠，是別人的名\n[Pre-Chorus]\n伊逐工來揣我食中晝\n我共石頭藏佇圍裙底\n[Chorus]\n惠雯，惠雯，我倒寫你的名\n倒寫的字，印出來才是正\n我的心事若有人用鏡來照\n就會當讀著，是你\n[Verse]\n第一百粒，我刻甲天光\n刀仔放落，手搭佇桌邊\n沾一下紅印泥，我先印佇我的手\n紅紅的字，正正在在\n[Bridge]\n我共這粒印送予你\n你蓋佇批尾，予人知\n[Chorus]\n惠雯，惠雯，這擺我刻著矣\n倒寫的字，印出來是正\n我的手掌心，有你的名\n予你用鏡來照，就讀會著\n[Outro]\n惠雯，惠雯\n我的手掌，攏是你的名",
